+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+## State
+
+- Project fitted out with RIGGING.md. Clean working tree.
+- Specs authored: 3 feature files (todos, editing, persistence-and-routing).
+- watchbill.json written with 8 ordered watches.
+
+## Blockers
+
+1. **Missing dependencies.** `todomvc-common` and `todomvc-app-css` are listed in RIGGING.md under ## Dependencies but are NOT in package.json. These are required by the app spec and referenced by the template HTML (base.css, base.js, index.css). Install via: `npm install todomvc-common todomvc-app-css`. This is a rigging blocker for Shipwright.
+
+2. **Template paths.** The template HTML references `node_modules/todomvc-common/base.css`, `node_modules/todomvc-app-css/index.css`, and `node_modules/todomvc-common/base.js`. These resolve only after the packages are installed.
+
+3. **Happy-dom tier.** Current RIGGING.md has tier `default: @logic` and policy `@logic - no external credentials required`. Since scenarios render DOM via happy-dom, the tier setup is sound. No additional tier needed.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- localStorage key: `todos-vanillajs` (vanilla JS framework name per spec).
+- Step definition approach: QM will author step definitions using happy-dom in Node.js, no real browser needed.
+- No routing library needed; vanilla JS handles hashchange events.
+
+## Next
+
+- Route to Shipwright to resolve dependency blocker (install todomvc-common, todomvc-app-css).
+- After dependency install, dispatch QM for verification work per watchbill order.
