@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+Feature: Todo editing
+  As a user
+  I want to edit existing todos
+  So that I can correct or update my task descriptions
+
+  Rule: Entering edit mode
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a todo label activates edit mode
+    Given the app has a todo item "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the label of "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo item has the class "editing"
+    And the edit input is focused and contains the text "Buy milk"
+
+  Rule: Saving an edit
+
+  Scenario: Saving an edit by pressing Enter
+    Given the app is editing the todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user changes the value to "Buy oat milk"
+    And presses Enter
+    Then the todo item displays the title "Buy oat milk"
+    And the todo item does not have the class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Saving an edit by blurring the input
+    Given the app is editing the todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user changes the value to "Buy oat milk"
+    And the edit input loses focus
+    Then the todo item displays the title "Buy oat milk"
+    And the todo item does not have the class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Trimming whitespace on save
+    Given the app is editing the todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user changes the value to "   Buy oat milk   "
+    And presses Enter
+    Then the todo item displays the title "Buy oat milk"
+
+  Scenario: Clearing the title during edit destroys the todo
+    Given the app is editing the todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user changes the value to ""
+    And presses Enter
+    Then the "Buy milk" todo is removed from the list
+
+  Rule: Cancelling an edit
+
+  Scenario: Pressing Escape discards changes and leaves edit mode
+    Given the app is editing the todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user changes the value to "Buy oat milk"
+    And presses Escape
+    Then the todo item displays the title "Buy milk"
+    And the todo item does not have the class "editing"
