@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+Feature: Todo persistence and routing
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to persist across page reloads and be filterable by route
+  So that my task list survives browser refreshes and I can focus on active or completed items
+
+  Rule: localStorage persistence
+
+  Scenario: Todos are saved to localStorage
+    Given the app has a todo item "Buy milk"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the "Buy milk" todo appears in the list
+
+  Scenario: Completed state is persisted
+    Given the app has a completed todo item "Buy milk"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the "Buy milk" todo has the class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Editing mode is not persisted
+    Given the app is editing the todo "Buy milk"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the "Buy milk" todo does not have the class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: localStorage uses the correct key format
+    Given the app has a todo item "Buy milk"
+    When the user inspects localStorage
+    Then the storage key "todos-vanillajs" exists with valid todo data
+
+  Rule: Routing
+
+  Scenario: Default route shows all todos
+    Given the app has both active and completed todos
+    When the URL hash is "#/"
+    Then all todos are shown in the list
+
+  Scenario: Active route filters to active todos only
+    Given the app has an active todo "Buy milk" and a completed todo "Paint fence"
+    When the URL hash is "#/active"
+    Then only "Buy milk" is shown in the list
+    And "Paint fence" is not shown
+
+  Scenario: Completed route filters to completed todos only
+    Given the app has an active todo "Buy milk" and a completed todo "Paint fence"
+    When the URL hash is "#/completed"
+    Then only "Paint fence" is shown in the list
+    And "Buy milk" is not shown
+
+  Scenario: Selected filter link has the "selected" class
+    Given the app is on the All route
+    When the user clicks the "Active" filter link
+    Then the "Active" filter link has the "selected" class
+    And the "All" filter link does not have the "selected" class
+
+  Scenario: Active filter is persisted on reload
+    Given the app is on the Active route
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the "Active" filter link has the "selected" class
+    And only active todos are shown
+
+  Scenario: Checking a todo in a filtered view hides it
+    Given the app is on the Active route with todos "Buy milk" and "Paint fence" where "Paint fence" is completed
+    When the user marks "Buy milk" as completed
+    Then "Buy milk" is removed from the visible list
+    And "Paint fence" is not shown either
+    And the todo-count displays "0" items left
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/features/todos.feature b/features/todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..dc70122
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,103 @@
+Feature: Todo management
+  As a user
+  I want to create, complete, and clear todos
+  So that I can track what needs to be done
+
+  Rule: No todos state
+
+  Scenario: Main and footer are hidden when there are no todos
+    Given the app is freshly loaded with no todos
+    Then the main section is not visible
+    And the footer is not visible
+
+  Rule: Creating a new todo
+
+  Scenario: User creates a todo
+    Given the app is freshly loaded with no todos
+    When the user types "Buy milk" into the new-todo input
+    And presses Enter
+    Then a new todo item appears in the list with the title "Buy milk"
+    And the new-todo input is cleared
+
+  Scenario: Trimming whitespace from a new todo title
+    Given the app is freshly loaded with no todos
+    When the user types "   Paint the fence   " into the new-todo input
+    And presses Enter
+    Then a new todo item appears in the list with the title "Paint the fence"
+
+  Scenario: Empty todo is not created
+    Given the app is freshly loaded with no todos
+    When the user types "" into the new-todo input
+    And presses Enter
+    Then no new todo item is created
+
+  Rule: Todo item interactions
+
+  Scenario: Checking a todo marks it as completed
+    Given the app has a todo item "Buy milk"
+    When the user clicks the checkbox on the "Buy milk" todo
+    Then the "Buy milk" todo has the class "completed"
+    And its checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Unchecking a completed todo marks it active
+    Given the app has a completed todo item "Buy milk"
+    When the user clicks the checkbox on the "Buy milk" todo
+    Then the "Buy milk" todo does not have the class "completed"
+    And its checkbox is not checked
+
+  Scenario: Hovering over a todo shows the remove button
+    Given the app has a todo item "Buy milk"
+    When the user hovers over the "Buy milk" todo
+    Then the destroy button on the "Buy milk" todo is visible
+
+  Rule: Mark all as complete
+
+  Scenario: Marking all todos as complete
+    Given the app has todo items "Buy milk" and "Paint fence"
+    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then every todo item has the class "completed"
+    And the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all clears when all items are individually checked
+    Given the app has todo items "Buy milk" and "Paint fence"
+    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    And the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox again
+    Then no todo item has the class "completed"
+    And the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all syncs with individual item state
+    Given the app has todo items "Buy milk" and "Paint fence"
+    When the user clicks the checkbox on "Buy milk"
+    And the user clicks the checkbox on "Paint fence"
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Clearing completed todos removes them
+    Given the app has a completed todo item "Buy milk" and an active todo "Paint fence"
+    When the user clicks the "Clear completed" button
+    Then the "Buy milk" todo is removed from the list
+    And the "Paint fence" todo remains in the list
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button is hidden when no todos are completed
+    Given the app has an active todo item "Paint fence"
+    When the user views the footer
+    Then the "Clear completed" button is not visible
+
+  Rule: Active todo counter
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows the number of active todos
+    Given the app has todo items "Buy milk" and "Paint fence"
+    When the user marks "Buy milk" as completed
+    Then the todo-count displays "1" item left
+
+  Scenario: Counter is pluralized for multiple active todos
+    Given the app has todo items "Buy milk", "Paint fence", and "Walk dog"
+    Then the todo-count displays "3" items left
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows zero when all todos are completed
+    Given the app has completed todo items "Buy milk" and "Paint fence"
+    Then the todo-count displays "0" items left
+
+  Scenario: Destroy button removes a single todo
+    Given the app has a todo item "Buy milk"
+    When the user clicks the destroy button on "Buy milk"
+    Then the "Buy milk" todo is removed from the list
\ No newline at end of file
